      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Advanced Personal Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Advanced Personal Trainer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S314P Working Title Advanced Personal Trainer FLSA Pay Grade Advertised Salary Position Status Casual (450 hours) Appointment Length 12 Months Department Wellness Center Job Summary/Basic Function Personal trainers guide and motivate clients to reach their peak fitness potential. Minimum Qualifications High School/ GED Equivalent CPR and First Aid certification Personal Trainer Certification (American College of Sports Medicine Preferred) Group Exercise Certification(s) (Aerobics and Fitness Association of America Preferred) Necessary skills include: Knowledge of the field of exercise science and prescription. Knowledge to develop and implement fitness regimens. Knowledge of proper use and care of many types of recreational equipment. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Analytical skills to identify problems, assess alternatives, and render consistent logical decisions in terms of health related issues. Ability to operate a personal computer with the knowledge of basic office software and software used to schedule events and facilities. Ability to collaborate effectively as a member of a goal oriented team. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse group of individuals. Excellent oral and written communication and customer service skills 1 year experience in development and/or execution of group Exercise Classes and PT Programs 1 year experience working in a high-volume recreational facility with demonstrated competency in customer service. Preferred Qualifications At least 1 year training experience in similar facility Posting Date 05/05/2025 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Job Duties Description of Job Duties Personal trainers guide and motivate clients to reach their peak fitness potential. · Conduct fitness consultations and assessments · Develop unique and individualized programs that ensure client safety, satisfaction, and enhancement of personal fitness goals · Assist, monitor, and instruct clients · Ensure safe and effective use of equipment · Maintain consistent client base · Provide exceptional customer service to members and guests throughout the SUWC · Assist with additional responsibilities as needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
