    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/16793": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal | Trades Specialist II/HVAC Tech",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Trades Specialist II/HVAC Tech Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Trades Specialist II/HVAC Tech Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S340P Working Title Trades Specialist II/HVAC Tech FLSA Non-Exempt Pay Grade 3 Advertised Salary Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department Facilities Management Job Summary/Basic Function The HVAC -R Technician will be involved in a wide variety of maintenance, repair, installation and service activities related to the mechanical systems of Shepherd University. Primary responsibilities include the maintenance and repair activities of HVAC -R systems. Developing and maintaining equipment repair and preventive maintenance schedules; maintaining HVAC operations efficiency through monitoring and calibration of controlling equipment and directing and monitoring repair activities of vendors supplying HVAC services to the university. Minimum Qualifications Job requires broad trade knowledge or specific technical or business knowledge received from a formal registered apprentice or vocational training program or obtained through an associates degree or over 18 months and up to 3 years beyond high school. Over two years of experience. Preferred Qualifications - Posting Date 08/25/2025 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o 13 paid holidays o 15 days annual leave (vacation) per year o 18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties Performs maintenance, repair, and replacement of air-moving, heating, cooling, humidification and filtering equipment and systems such as fans, heat pumps, fan coil units, rooftop package air conditioning units, humidistat, pressure and volume controls. Systems include reciprocating and centrifugal type and include related electrical motors and their respective controls, including calibration of equipment, gauges and controls, handling of refrigerant and charging systems. Providing over site and direction to contract vendors engaged in HVAC repairs. Monitoring the EMS and mechanical control systems for optimal operating efficiency. Adjusts systems control parameters as required and responds to systems failures as determined. Performs installation or modification work on heating and cooling systems and controls, including planning the work; estimating and arranging the materials, supplies and equipment required; and coordination with other trades. Maintaining, repairing, and replacing hot water, condenser and chilled water systems, including pumps, control valves, coils, heat exchangers, cooling towers and related controls. Maintains and repairs fume hoods. Maintains repairs and replaces low-pressure boilers used for heating and cooling of air and their combustion and control systems. Maintaining an inventory of replacement parts and supplies to support repair and maintenance of HVAC -R systems. Maintaining assigned tools, vehicles and equipment. Rotates in on the On-Call Trades Schedule responding to emergency and urgent work requests in the off schedule hours. Holds on-call phone and remains ready to respond to requests. Assists in snow clearing operations with other essential employees. Other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
