    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18466": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Athletic Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Athletic Trainer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S405P Working Title Athletic Trainer FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Non-Classified Advertised Salary $50,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department Athletics Job Summary/Basic Function This is an 12-month appointment for a certified Athletic Trainer. The athletic trainer is responsible for helping provide medical services to 15 Division II athletic teams. Minimum Qualifications BOC Certified Athletic Trainer Bachelor’s Degree CPR certification Eligible for West Virginia State Licensure Effective verbal and written communication skills Ability to work effectively in a team setting. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred Experience working with a collegiate football program Posting Date 05/21/2026 Close Date 06/19/2026 Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o 13 paid holidays o 24 days annual leave (vacation) per year o 18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties Provide comprehensive medical services to athletic teams as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer, Assist with supervision of practices and games. Assist the Head Athletic Trainer with all EMR information for student-athletes. Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in help with student-workers and intern students. Electronic documentation of all patient encounters. Communicate with physicians and coaching staff regarding injury status of athletes. Minor tasks may include: Assist the Head Athletic Trainer in purchasing, budgeting, and maintenance of supplies and equipment for the athletic training facility. Assist in a clean environment in the athletic training room. Assist in other duties as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer and/or Athletic Director. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18537": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Dean College of Business and Technology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Dean College of Business and Technology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S409P Working Title Dean College of Business and Technology FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Non-Classified Advertised Salary Beginning at $160,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department HR Job Postings Job Summary/Basic Function The Dean of Business and Technology provides strategic leadership and manages all operational aspects of the College. The dean collaboratively leads a dedicated faculty in delivering high-quality academic programs that support student and faculty success across the College and University. Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree in business administration, economics, accounting, recreation, sport management, computer science, mathematics, computer engineering, or related field from a regionally accredited institution. Five (5) years of progressively higher administrative responsibilities with a proven track record in program development, grant funding, external engagement, and assessment and accreditation. Sufficient evidence of teaching, research, and service as appropriate for a tenured full professor in the college. Demonstrated success in attracting, recruiting, retaining, and evaluating faculty. Proven track record of mentoring and providing professional development support to faculty and staff. Success in developing and managing a fiscally sound unit budget that aligns with strategic priorities. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated success in building innovative academic programs that scale. Commitment to student success with concrete examples of innovative initiatives that improve retention, persistence, and graduation rates. Experience and understanding of the development and delivery of quality online instruction. Demonstrated experience in integrating emerging technologies and sustainability initiatives into academic programs and operations (e.g., generative AI, online pedagogy, etc.). Experience in collaboratively leading the development and delivery of strategic objectives. Demonstrated success in fostering interdisciplinary collaboration across academic programs and departments within the University to support innovation, shared resources, and student success. Posting Date 06/01/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits, including: 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match. Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents. Eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement. Applications must include a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, a leadership philosophy (maximum three pages), and five names of professional references with email addresses and telephone numbers. Nominations and confidential inquiries may be sent to Ms. Tammy Gill, director of human resources/ CHRO , at tgill@shepherd.edu . To be guaranteed consideration, candidates must submit their application materials by August 1, 2026. Job Duties Description of Job Duties The Dean of Business and Technology provides strategic leadership and manages all operational aspects of the College. The dean collaboratively leads a dedicated faculty in delivering high-quality academic programs that support student and faculty success across the College and University. The following is a summation of the dean’s most essential job responsibilities: Collaboratively leads a dedicated team of faculty and staff in the development of strategic objectives that support teaching excellence, student success, enrollment growth, and program innovation within the College. Supervises, mentors, and evaluates unit leaders, faculty, and administrative staff. Builds working relationships with internal and external stakeholders, advocating for resources necessary to support academic programs, faculty, and staff. Identifies market opportunities for new and/or revised programs in the College, facilitating the curricular development of degrees, certificates, and micro-credentials that meet market demand and prepare students for professional success. Identifies and secures external funding through grants, external partnerships, and donors to support the strategic objectives of the College. Recruits and retains talented faculty and staff to support the academic mission of the College. Oversees the facilitation and execution of assessment processes for accreditation and Board of Governors program reviews. Promotes professional and community outreach projects and activities. Collects and maintains data for assessment of students, graduates, and academic programs. Develops an annual budget for the College and administers the allocated budget according to institutional guidelines. Develops sustainable partnerships and programmatic pathways with institutions in the region and across West Virginia. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document 1 List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18731": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Campus Police Investigator I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus Police Investigator I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S415P Working Title Campus Police Investigator I FLSA Non-Exempt Pay Grade 6 Advertised Salary $25.64 without WV Certification/$30.77 with WV Certification Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department University Police Job Summary/Basic Function The Campus Police Investigator I is responsible for maintaining the safety and security of the university community and campus facilities through proactive patrol, enforcement of state laws and university policies, and emergency response services. This position exercises law enforcement authority to protect individuals and property from harm, loss, or damage; responds to calls for service; conducts investigations; and supports a safe and secure learning environment through professional and community-oriented policing practices. Minimum Qualifications Available to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and special events. Ability to learn and work with computer database systems. Not later than first day of employment, must hold a valid driver’s license and successfully meet all minimum requirements of WV Code 30-29-1 et. seq . as to standards for law enforcement officers of West Virginia. Must either have current police officer certification in WV or be eligible as to all Academy Entry Standards (including health and fitness) at the time of hire [ http://www.dcjs.wv.gov/law-enforcement-training/Documents/149CSR2.pdf ]. This includes the National Fire Protection Association 1582 Medical Selection Guidelines. Preferred Qualifications Current West Virginia Law Enforcement Certification preferred Graduation from an accredited police academy and possession of a valid law enforcement certification Prior campus law enforcement, public safety, or related law enforcement experience preferred Posting Date 07/09/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work.  Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o   13 paid holidays o   15 days annual leave (vacation) per year o   18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o   Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o   401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o   Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties Exercises general law enforcement authority to protect life and property and to prevent injury, harm, theft, vandalism, and criminal activity on university property. Patrols campus property by foot and vehicle to maintain a visible police presence and enforce state laws and university regulations. Monitors campus traffic and parking operations and issues warnings or citations for violations in accordance with established procedures and policies. Responds to emergencies, calls for service, alarms, accidents, suspicious activity, and other incidents requiring law enforcement assistance. Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations of criminal and non-criminal incidents and initiates appropriate action in accordance with university policy and applicable federal, state, and local laws. Prepares and maintains accurate written reports, incident documentation, accident reports, citations, and other law enforcement records; performs data entry and updates within departmental software systems. Reports fires, safety hazards, utility failures, attempted unlawful entry, and other threats to persons or property, and takes appropriate action to minimize damage and ensure public safety. Assists local, state, and federal law enforcement agencies as needed in matters involving or adjacent to university property. Identifies, apprehends, arrests, and assists in the prosecution of individuals involved in criminal violations. May assist with training activities, special events, crowd management, and other duties as assigned in support of departmental operations. Provides assistance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors, including motorist assistance, escorts, and other public safety services Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18927": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Casual employee - Athletic Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Casual employee - Athletic Trainer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S419P Working Title Casual employee - Athletic Trainer FLSA Pay Grade Advertised Salary Position Status Casual (450 hours) Appointment Length 12 Months Department Athletic Trainers Job Summary/Basic Function This position is responsible for the day-to-day oversight of athletic training services for multiple NCAA Div. II Olympic Sports programs. The position will also coordinate student-athlete insurance reconciliations and support institutional summer camp coverage. Minimum Qualifications High School/ GED Equivalent CPR and First Aid certification Personal Trainer Certification (American College of Sports Medicine Preferred) Group Exercise Certification(s) (Aerobics and Fitness Association of America Preferred) Necessary skills include: Knowledge of the field of exercise science and prescription. Knowledge to develop and implement fitness regimens. Knowledge of proper use and care of many types of recreational equipment. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Analytical skills to identify problems, assess alternatives, and render consistent logical decisions in terms of health related issues. Ability to operate a personal computer with the knowledge of basic office software and software used to schedule events and facilities. Ability to collaborate effectively as a member of a goal oriented team. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse group of individuals. Excellent oral and written communication and customer service skills 1 year experience in development and/or execution of group Exercise Classes and PT Programs 1 year experience working in a high-volume recreational facility with demonstrated competency in customer service. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred Experience working with a collegiate athletics setting Posting Date 08/06/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Job Duties Description of Job Duties Sports Coverage and Clinical Athletic Training Responsibilities Primary athletic training coverage for the multiple Olympic sports; Assist with the prevention and care of athletic related injuries for all sports programs; Provide evaluation, treatment and rehabilitation of injuries and illnesses under the general supervision of the head athletic trainer and team physician; Maintain current certification and credentials consistent with NATA ; BOC certified; Certified to practice in West Virginia and CPR / AED certified; Maintain accurate and up-to-date written treatment and injury records; Provide regular communication with coaching staff regarding injury and participation status of student-athletes; Modest travel required in support of primary sport(s) Administrative Responsibilities Assist in the improvement and assimilation of sports medicine policies and procedures; Assist with all aspects of inventory control; Verify and document that University and NCAA insurance requirements are met for student-athletes; Coordination and oversight of athletic training coverage for institutional summer camps; Prepare, record and retain documentation as required; Perform other duties as assigned; Report any knowledge of rules violations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
