 and university regulations. Monitors campus traffic and parking operations and issues warnings or citations for violations in accordance with established procedures and policies. Responds to emergencies, calls for service, alarms, accidents, suspicious activity, and other incidents requiring law enforcement assistance. Conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations of criminal and non-criminal incidents and initiates appropriate action in accordance with university policy and applicable federal, state, and local laws. Prepares and maintains accurate written reports, incident documentation, accident reports, citations, and other law enforcement records; performs data entry and updates within departmental software systems. Reports fires, safety hazards, utility failures, attempted unlawful entry, and other threats to persons or property, and takes appropriate action to minimize damage and ensure public safety. Assists local, state, and federal law enforcement agencies as needed in matters involving or adjacent to university property. Identifies, apprehends, arrests, and assists in the prosecution of individuals involved in criminal violations. May assist with training activities, special events, crowd management, and other duties as assigned in support of departmental operations. Provides assistance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors, including motorist assistance, escorts, and other public safety services Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
