    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/16721": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal | Trades Specialist II/Plumber",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Trades Specialist II/Plumber Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Trades Specialist II/Plumber Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S352P Working Title Trades Specialist II/Plumber FLSA Non-Exempt Pay Grade 3 Advertised Salary $46,163 ($23.67/hr) - $55,395 ($28.41/hr) Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department Facilities Management Job Summary/Basic Function The plumber/oil-burner technician will be involved in a variety of repairs, maintenance, and service and installation activities related to maintaining Shepherd University mechanical systems. Must be able to respond to emergency situations on all occasions and must be available for telephone contact during all emergency and environmentally unsafe conditions. Minimum Qualifications Job requires broad trade knowledge or specific technical or business knowledge received from a formal registered apprentice or vocational training program or obtained through an associates degree or over 18 months and up to 3 years beyond high school. Over two years of experience. Preferred Qualifications Posting Date 10/02/2025 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o 13 paid holidays o 15 days annual leave (vacation) per year o 18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties Maintains, repairs, and replaces sprinkler systems, including piping and related supports, sprinkler heads, control valves, pumps and fixtures. Must be able to respond to emergency situations on all occasions and must be available for telephone contact during all emergency and environmentally unsafe conditions. Other duties as assigned. Performs minor installation or modification work on liquid distribution systems including planning the work, estimating, ordering materials and supplies and equipment required to perform the work. Coordinates with other tradesmen as needed. Repairs and replaces piping in non-potable water systems such as condenser and chiller water systems as required to support the HVAC technician. Maintains, repairs, and replaces low-pressure steam systems, including boilers, control valves, piping, pumps, fittings, heat exchangers, controls, traps, meters, and other associated components. Maintains, repairs, and replaces oil-burners and related controls and components. Maintains repairs and replaces heat piping, radiation and pumps. Maintains, repairs, and replaces potable water systems made from metal or plastic including piping and related supports, fixtures such as faucets and toilets, fittings, pumps, hot water tanks, valves, meters, backflow preventers, controls and related softeners, distillers, booster pumps and safety showers. Maintains, repairs, and replaces sewage and storm water systems made from metal or plastic, including piping, vents and required supports for liquids such as sewage, storm water runoff, acids, solvents and other lab wastes. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18013": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Wellness Center Flex Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Wellness Center Flex Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S146P Working Title Wellness Center Flex Manager FLSA Pay Grade Advertised Salary Position Status Casual (450 hours) Appointment Length Other Department Wellness Center Job Summary/Basic Function The Flex Supervisor will be responsible daily operation of all areas of the facility and supervision of student staff. This position will oversee all areas of the facility including financial, risk management and equipment responsibilities. In lieu of the professional staff, this individual will be responsible for facility operation and will have all current certification(s) and training necessary to do so. Minimum Qualifications Job requires broad trade knowledge or specific technical or business knowledge received from a formal registered apprentice or vocational training program or obtained through an associates degree or over 18 months and up to 3 years beyond high school. Over two years of experience. Preferred Qualifications Professional Rescuers CPR , and/or Lifeguarding Certification Certified Pool Operator Water Safety Instructor Group Exercise or Personal Training Certification Weight Fitness Experienced 1 year employment at the Wellness Center Posting Date 10/25/2022 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18469": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S400P Working Title Counselor FLSA Exempt Pay Grade 4 Advertised Salary starting at $53,910 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 11 Months Department Counseling Job Summary/Basic Function This individual’s primary responsibility will be to provide direct services to the student population in various areas of mental health support including individual and group counseling, educational workshops, prevention, outreach, and training. The counselor will participate on the Behavioral Intervention Team to address the needs of students at risk. The counselor will collaborate with campus partners on prevention program development, campus outreach, and participate in other projects presented by Counseling Services or the Division of Student Affairs. The counselor may serve as a representative on campus coalitions, including the Crisis Response Team, and/or represent Counseling Services on various committees serving the student-body. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in counseling, social work, or related field. Independent clinical license in counseling or social work or graduate license with eligibility to work toward clinical licensure under direct supervision. Direct counseling experience with individuals and groups on diverse topics. Preferred Qualifications 5+ years counseling experience, preferably with adolescents and young adults Experience with acute psychiatric conditions Experience with acute crisis intervention, risk assessments and safety planning Experience with case management and resource development Knowledge, cultural humility, and experience supporting students who identify as BIPOC , LGBTQIA+, and neurodiverse Promotion of social justice, equity, and inclusion practices Experience with development and implementation of prevention programming, mental health promotion, and trauma informed care Excellent written and verbal communication necessary for documentation, campus collaboration and the development of program materials including social media content Adaptability to meet evolving needs of students Posting Date 05/21/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o 13 paid holidays o 24 days annual leave (vacation) per year o 18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties This individual’s primary responsibility will be to provide direct services to the student population in various areas of mental health support including individual and group counseling, educational workshops, prevention, outreach, and training. The counselor will participate on the Behavioral Intervention Team to address the needs of students at risk. The counselor will collaborate with campus partners on prevention program development, campus outreach, and participate in other projects presented by Counseling Services or the Division of Student Affairs. The counselor may serve as a representative on campus coalitions, including the Crisis Response Team, and/or represent Counseling Services on various committees serving the student-body. Other duties as assigned Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs-shepherd.peopleadmin.com/postings/18684": {
      "title": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Director of Facilities Management",
      "description": "Shepherd University Portal | Assistant Director of Facilities Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Facilities Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Information Posting Number S412P Working Title Assistant Director of Facilities Management FLSA Exempt Pay Grade Non-Classified Advertised Salary $85,000 - $93,000 Position Status Full Time Appointment Length 12 Months Department Facilities Management Job Summary/Basic Function This position leads daily facility maintenance operations, supervising trades and custodial staff while managing both scheduled and reactive work. Oversees CMMS work orders to ensure timely completion and coordinates preventive, routine, and emergency repairs. Supports budgeting, vendor oversight, and project documentation while monitoring contractor performance. Ensures regulatory compliance, manages campus safety programs and training, and assists leadership in maintaining and improving facilities. Minimum Qualifications Bachelors degree in Engineering, Engineering Technology, Safety, Project Management or related field of study. Or. Associates degree and 4+ years of relevant experience in facilities management, project/construction management or industrial safety. OSHA 10 Preferred Qualifications OSHA Certified Instructor MBA or Masters of Engineering 10+ years of experience in commercial or industrial facilities maintenance or construction. LEED AP Posting Date 06/30/2026 Close Date Special Instructions Summary Appointment to this position will be contingent upon a satisfactory background check. We believe in work-life balance and keeping time for things we love outside our work. Shepherd University offers generous employee benefits , including: o 13 paid holidays o 24 days annual leave (vacation) per year o 18 sick days per year and the flexibility to use that time to care for immediate family members o Wide range of health insurance and other benefits o 401(a) retirement savings with 6% contribution match; eligibility to continue health insurance post-retirement, and other retiree perks o Tuition waivers for employees and their dependents Job Duties Description of Job Duties Manage daily operations of facility maintenance, both scheduled and reactive. Supervise and coordinate work across skilled trades and custodial services. Respond to/manage/resolve employee, vendor and administrative concerns. Utilize the CMMS to create, monitor, prioritize and ensure timely completion of work orders in accordance with University standards. Assist in the development and execution of departmental budgets, including monitoring expenses and identifying cost-saving initiatives. Participates in the preparation and submission of project reports, change orders, construction change directives, meeting minutes and other records necessary to administer projects and document the work performed. Supervises, inspects and monitors work being performed by outside vendors and contractors. Coordinates scheduling and supervision of routine, preventative and emergency repairs to facilities and equipment. Assists the Director of Facilities Management in the planning, organization, and direction of staff in the upkeep of all University grounds and buildings. Responds to emergency calls on a 24 hr basis and disseminate the proper staff to mitigate the emergency. Provide support to emergency response personnel with technical, hazardous chemical and emergency protocol information. Oversee and enforce Environmental, Health and Safety compliance with applicable regulations ( OSHA , ASHRAE , NFPA , NEC , DEP , EPA , etc) Develop and maintain a system for the handling, collection, storage and disposal of hazardous, bio-hazard and universal waste across campus. Direct the work of other safety personnel throughout campus as required. Perform and/or schedule staff safety training and maintain documentation of training and safety incidents campus wide. Respond to regulatory agencies for compliance documentation. Make recommendations to improve existing equipment and processes. Provides backup to the Director of Facilities Management as authorized. Performs other duties and assignments as requested by the Director of Facilities Management Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of Professional References Optional Documents VISIT 301 N KING ST, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 MAIL P.O. BOX 5000, SHEPHERDSTOWN, WV  25443 CALL 304.876.5000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
